#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD2246 expect=violation domain=TS
#note "A count of planned arms is a whole number: '2.5' is numeric but not an integer, and the authored rule (Description/Message: 'numeric (integer)') flags it. Pins the deliberate integer reading of the sheet's 'must be numeric'. (Positive control added by PLAN-absent-guard-test-hardening P3: PMDA-SD2246 previously had ONLY an expect=skipped fixture, which asserts non-execution and so proved nothing about the rule ever running. Modelled on its twin FDA-SD2246.)"
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 TSPARMCD=NARMS TSVAL=2.5
dataset TS label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | TS | 1 | NARMS | Planned Number of Arms | 2.5
